On 2003-11-21, Zwanth <zwanth@sunflower.com> wrote:
>
> Perhaps a new dragon could be made.  I will call it... the Shimmering
> Dragon.
> Shimmering dragon scale mail would confer a random intrinsic every
> game, based on a list of unusual intrinsics:

I don't like the idea of a DSM conveying random intrinsics.  Assigning
some of the suggested intrinsics to various dragons might make other
suits more attractive though. (some items were juggled around)

> amphibiousness
> unbreathing

Amphibiousness suits white dragons the most, since it's closest to a
water dragon.  I think having it causes eels to not even attempt
drowning attacks, so WDSM could be an alternative to oilskin.
However, you can still choke, unless it also conveys unbreathing.

> displacement

This is what shimmering dragons would convey if displacement for
enemies were implemented.  Displacement is nice to have.

> level-drain resistance

These days I try to keep my level low, after the Quest, but some other
people may want it.  Black dragons appears most appropriate for some
reason, possibly because of Stormy.

> hallucination resistance
> protection from shape changers
> sustain ability

I don't see any of these as being useful in the late game.
Hallucination resistance is easily fixed, shape shifters aren't any
trouble, and IMHO sustain ability isn't a good thing.

> stoning resistance (maybe too powerful)

Yes, much too powerful.

Also, if orange dragon scales conveyed free action, it would probably
be chosen more.  And if there were more nasty acidic monsters, yellow
DSM might be more popular.

Red/blue DSM could absorb fire/lightning damage (like Chrono Trigger)
to make them more attractive.  Perhaps they could protect items from
burning/exploding, since merely absorbing damage seems insufficient.
That could allow people wearing RDSM to sit on fire traps and heal.

Now the only DSM without anything special is green.  Probably give it
ESP and warning, just because they are useful.

